index 302b779..c7d4401 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -136,6 +136,18 @@ Set `PROCEDURA_REFERENCE_ROOT` to a directory outside the Procedura checkout
 and outputs root. Studio uses the same setting to display the imported Mesh;
 the run directory stores only an opaque `reference.json` descriptor.
 
+After import is verified, controlled observation can produce a reconstruction
+brief without generating CAD:
+
+```bash
+bun run mesh-to-cad --observe-only --mesh reference.stl \
+  -o outputs/reference-observation
+```
+
+The Observer receives only a bounded summary and fixed isometric/front/right/top
+PNG views. Dimensions and view mappings in `reconstruction-brief.json` are
+written by the host, not accepted from the model.
+
 That is text-only, part-by-part, with no image API and no Blender in the draft
 loop, and it is what you get with no flags at all. It is the cheapest useful
 configuration, not the strongest one.
